---
---
<section class="section section-bg-white" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="heading-lg">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Everything you need to know about memberships, hours, parking, and building access.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-container">
      
      <div class="faq-item active">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <span>How does the 1-Day Free Pass work?</span>
          <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Simply fill out the Free Day Pass form on our homepage. We will send you a digital pass. You can drop in anytime Monday through Friday between 8:30 AM and 5:00 PM to work for the day, enjoy our craft coffee, and test our high-speed wifi.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <span>What are the building access hours?</span>
          <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Dedicated Desk and Private Office members enjoy 24/7/365 secure keycard access to the building. Day Pass and Hot Desk members have access during staffed office hours from 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM, Monday through Friday.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <span>Are contracts long-term or month-to-month?</span>
          <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          We believe in total flexibility! All our memberships are available on a simple month-to-month agreement. We also offer discounted rates for teams committing to 6-month or 12-month leases.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <span>Where can members and guests park?</span>
          <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          We are located in the heart of Denver CBD at 1514 Curtis Street. Numerous parking garages are situated within 1 block of our building, and we are just steps away from the 16th Street Mall shuttle and RTD Light Rail stations.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <span>Can I bring clients or guests to meetings?</span>
          <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes! Members can host guests in booked conference rooms or kitchen lounge areas. All conference room bookings include guest access, high-speed wifi, and complimentary coffee/tea.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.faq-container {
  max-width: 800px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1rem;
}

.faq-item {
  background: #FFFFFF;
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.faq-question {
  padding: 1.4rem 1.8rem;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-family: var(--font-heading);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  color: var(--dark-navy);
  user-select: none;
}

.faq-question i {
  color: var(--primary-red);
  transition: transform var(--transition-fast);
}

.faq-item.active .faq-question i {
  transform: rotate(180deg);
}

.faq-answer {
  max-height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: max-height 0.35s ease, padding 0.35s ease;
  padding: 0 1.8rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: 0.95rem;
}

.faq-item.active .faq-answer {
  max-height: 250px;
  padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
}
</style>

<script>
  const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item');
  faqItems.forEach(item => {
    const question = item.querySelector('.faq-question');
    if (question) {
      question.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const isActive = item.classList.contains('active');
        faqItems.forEach(other => other.classList.remove('active'));
        if (!isActive) {
          item.classList.add('active');
        }
      });
    }
  });
</script>
